---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import OriginalIndex from '../components/OriginalIndex.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/constants.mjs';
import walkthroughs from '../data/walkthroughs.json';

const firstRequestStep = walkthroughs.request[0].id;

const indexEntries = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview', description: 'One assistant, clear service boundaries' },
  { id: 'request-path', label: 'Request workflow', description: 'Coordination handles inference and retrieval' },
  { id: 'system-map', label: 'Architecture', description: 'Browser UI, gateway, retrieval, and state' },
  { id: 'manual-ingestion', label: 'Manual ingestion', description: 'Preparation runs outside the conversation' },
  { id: 'decisions-tradeoffs', label: 'Decisions', description: 'Tradeoffs and the decisions route' }
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Architecture — Nora SuperIntelligence Lab" description="System architecture for the Nora knowledge assistant: Browser UI, Coordination, and MCP gateway with clear service boundaries." path="/architecture/" customIndex={true}>
  <section class="hero" id="overview" data-index-label="Overview">
    <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow--one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow--two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="shell hero-layout">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>One assistant. Clear service boundaries.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Architecture shows the reusable system: who owns each responsibility, how a request moves, and why document preparation stays outside the conversation. The walkthrough applies those same boundaries to concrete scenarios.</p>
        <p class="hero-snapshot"><strong>Published Harness snapshot:</strong> MCP clients use the LiteLLM gateway. <a href={href('/case-study/evolution/')}>See the later direct-API design</a>.</p>
        <ul class="hero-signals" aria-label="Design principles">
          <li>Single assistant</li>
          <li>Prepared knowledge</li>
          <li>Durable state</li>
          <li>Provider-flexible</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions hero-actions--foundation">
          <a class="button button--primary" href={href(`/walkthroughs/?flow=request&step=${firstRequestStep}`)}>Follow the request path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="button button--ghost" href="https://github.com/lm2000/nora-ai-knowledge-agent-harness-public/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nora source on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <OriginalIndex tagline="Architecture" entries={indexEntries} ariaLabel="Architecture navigation" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="request-path" data-index-label="Workflow">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Request workflow</p>
          <h2 id="request-path-heading">How one request reaches an answer.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>This reusable request path is the system contract: the question enters through the Browser UI or embedded tool, Coordination retrieves prepared passages, and the answer is produced while the checkpoint is retained. The walkthrough applies it to the fictional Atlas question.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="request-path-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/architecture-request-path-preview.svg"
          title="Request path"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/architecture-request-path.html"
          alt="Architecture request path diagram"
          caption="The request path shows how Coordination handles inference and retrieval directly."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="system-map" data-index-label="Architecture" aria-labelledby="system-map-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Technical architecture</p>
          <h2 id="system-map-heading">Components, state, and system boundaries.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The map makes ownership explicit. Browser UI connects directly to Coordination, while MCP clients separately use the gateway to embedded FastMCP; Retrieval and conversation state remain separate services.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="architecture-version">This diagram shows the pinned public Harness snapshot, where MCP clients use the LiteLLM gateway. <a href={href('/case-study/evolution/')}>Compare the later direct-API design</a>.</p>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="system-map-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          title="System architecture"
          previewSrc="/diagrams/01-system-architecture-preview.svg"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/01-system-architecture.html"
          alt="System architecture diagram showing Browser UI AG-UI connects directly to Coordination. MCP clients separately use LiteLLM MCP gateway to embedded FastMCP or direct FastMCP."
          caption="Browser UI connects directly to Coordination, while MCP clients separately use the gateway to embedded FastMCP."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="manual-ingestion" data-index-label="Ingestion" aria-labelledby="manual-ingestion-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Manual ingestion</p>
          <h2 id="manual-ingestion-heading">Preparation stays outside the conversation.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Conversion, preparation, embedding, and import are operator-triggered jobs, not request-time work. This separate path prepares documents and the retrieval index; the walkthrough shows it as its own operator scenario.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="manual-ingestion-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/manual-ingestion-preview.svg"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/manual-ingestion.html"
          title="Manual ingestion"
          alt="Manual ingestion pipeline diagram"
          caption="Manual ingestion runs outside the conversation flow to prepare text for retrieval."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section foundation-section" id="decisions-tradeoffs" data-index-label="Decisions">
    <div class="shell foundation-layout">
      <div class="foundation-copy">
        <p class="section-label">Decisions &amp; tradeoffs</p>
        <h2>Architecture decisions and tradeoffs.</h2>
        <p>Architecture defines the reusable boundaries. Decisions records why they were chosen, Validation records what was checked, and Walkthroughs applies the boundaries to concrete examples.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={href('/decisions/')}>Review decisions and tradeoffs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <nav class="architecture-related" aria-label="Architecture related reading">
        <h3 id="purpose">Conversation contract</h3>
        <p>What the assistant is for and how it answers: see the <a href={href('/decisions/')}>accepted conversation contract</a> on the Decisions page.</p>
        <h3 id="example">Concrete walkthrough</h3>
        <p>See the fictional Atlas request and operator ingestion scenarios in <a href={href(`/walkthroughs/?flow=request&step=${firstRequestStep}`)}>Walkthroughs</a>.</p>
        <h3 id="approach-and-tradeoffs">Accepted decisions</h3>
        <p>Model routing, request bounds, and ingestion ownership: read the <a href={href('/decisions/')}>accepted execution decisions</a>.</p>
        <h3 id="boundaries-and-recovery">Evidence and limits</h3>
        <p>What was checked and what remains open: see <a href={href('/validation/')}>known limits and bounded follow-up</a>.</p>
        <h3>Workflows</h3>
        <p>See how <a href={href('/workflows/')}>artifact evaluation and revision</a> adds task-specific LLM feedback and human decisions alongside knowledge workflows.</p>
        <h3>How NIS was built</h3>
        <p>Read the <a href={href('/case-study/')}>engineering build story</a>: the problem, architectural alternatives, AI-assisted implementation and evidence.</p>
        <h3 id="reference">Run the source</h3>
        <p>Run the checks yourself: <a href={href('/reproduce/')}>reproduction commands</a>. Read the <a href="https://github.com/lm2000/nora-ai-knowledge-agent-harness-public/blob/10bd370c711afabdfc7b23b516911c31ff58bcb4/architecture/Architecture%20Concept.md">pinned architecture concept</a>.</p>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.hero-snapshot {
  max-width: 65ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
.hero-snapshot strong { color: var(--ink); }
.architecture-version {
  max-width: 70ch;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  line-height: 1.6;
}
.architecture-related {
  max-width: 38ch;
}
.architecture-related h3 {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  margin: 1.4em 0 0.35em;
  color: var(--ink);
  scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 24px);
}
.architecture-related h3:first-child {
  margin-top: 0;
}
.architecture-related p {
  color: #a6bac6;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.7;
  margin: 0;
}
.architecture-related a {
  color: var(--color-muted-blue);
}
.architecture-related a:hover {
  color: var(--teal-light);
}
</style>
